{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "03YC", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'E"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-etale}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:71f425c148ab07f88d4540823b113d81759f3c88c1a500f58a640f08120b6ebf", "source_text": "<ACCENT_0001>tale topology", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a0d758d4165dbe970fa4dbc68d69fb56e9238e57d5a24042d90c5820e510b669", "unit_id": "tag:03YC:title"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03YC", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-section-etale}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:54061b30e66087c39ca6e40690dd5acce776eea4f169d3fd8d508223a678bef1", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we discuss the notion of a <ACCENT_0001>tale covering of\nalgebraic spaces, and we define the big <ACCENT_0002>tale site of an\nalgebraic space. Please compare with\nTopologies, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:113d386499d5ba80b06f905485a97e4ac17c472b8536b764e06bddc2c3fbb16d", "unit_id": "tag:03YC:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03YC", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{f_i : X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$f_i$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n|X| = \\bigcup\\nolimits_{i \\in I} |f_i|(|X_i|),\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-etale-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e76fae56c3226e3151fabee0092a70b466b5acf08f6f31c1ff32db92d85286f7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:273c9018184dabdf84e46ce9506fbcb0f94638953ee723a87056f22392f7f154", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme, and let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nAn <TEXTITOPEN_0001><ACCENT_0001>tale covering of <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a family of morphisms\n<MATH_0005> of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0006>\nsuch that each <MATH_0007> is <ACCENT_0002>tale\nand such that\n<MATH_0008>\ni.e., the morphisms are jointly surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3388773550fc605e50e1b7527f1e18bc35f487a3b58bd234cde8eb15fdd981cd", "unit_id": "tag:041E:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03YC", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X_i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-definition-etale-covering}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:471134057d0984d44af5a155ac2d0e8da290e691491a26f5be3167e4b5c64d48", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7696fa9b7cc88ad9a1d0448d6c4cac7216648d9dd9c5420ce8749796cef0f5c6", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is exactly the same as\nTopologies, Definition <REF_0001>.\nIn particular, if <MATH_0001> and all the <MATH_0002> are schemes, then we recover the\nusual notion of a <ACCENT_0001>tale covering of schemes.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f70464e08d4307133b9d77f2d0f62ffa3f284227f447f65dfb3404dc894ee529", "unit_id": "tag:03YC:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03YC", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski-etale}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e015e2c3454b0567bd15a72f151683c581e8c39c3328125db00ca8d532ed6a8d", "source_text": "Any Zariski covering is an <ACCENT_0001>tale covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:14e5f0673c4ca70ba01f59403030e111b476623c4b1d9b5efc45527632643802", "unit_id": "tag:0DF1:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03YC", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-open-immersion-etale}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-lemma-representable-transformations-property-implication}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c42dae24da373e695773d5f4e27d5807f79fa74404910b95623f2f86769e4590", "source_text": "This is clear from the definitions and the fact that an open immersion\nis an <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism (this follows from\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0001> via\nSpaces, Lemma\n<REF_0002>\nas immersions are representable).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9394f8df14eef8bed1e1b6de64267ec148fe195cc1ad25e18d77fbd194b504d1", "unit_id": "tag:0DF1:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03YC", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0004": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0005": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0006": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X' \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{X' \\to X\\}$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0008": "$i$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{X_{ij} \\to X_i\\}_{j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\{X_{ij} \\to X\\}_{i \\in I, j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0012": "$X' \\to X$", "MATH_0013": "$\\{X' \\times_X X_i \\to X'\\}_{i\\in I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e3d9a30bc295880eafea81ddede5c59549b2394c91422582e284bba1fee4680", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5e34665a5930e405159e58a5c1912f7e9f92ce4f8edd7f0636c1e4368c175eee", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0004> is an isomorphism then <MATH_0005>\nis a <ACCENT_0001>tale covering of <MATH_0006>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0007> is a <ACCENT_0002>tale covering and for each\n<MATH_0008> we have a <ACCENT_0003>tale covering <MATH_0009>, then\n<MATH_0010> is a <ACCENT_0004>tale covering.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0011> is a <ACCENT_0005>tale covering\nand <MATH_0012> is a morphism of algebraic spaces then\n<MATH_0013> is a <ACCENT_0006>tale covering.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7d194a941bd59da0accdb0da98dbfe384705938166527af2aca004cdcd3f6108", "unit_id": "tag:041F:statement"}
